  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at the 9:30 Club in Washington, DC, on November 27, 2009 [1]. The concert was part of the band's initial North American tour to support their new record, The Life of the World to Come [1]. For this specific leg of the tour, the group’s usual three-piece lineup was expanded to include Perry Owen Wright on electric guitar [1]. The setlist features eighteen songs, totaling eighty-one minutes of music [1]. Several tracks in the performance are notable for their rarity in the archive, including Hebrews 11:14, which has only two archived performances, and It's All Here in Brownsville, with four [2]. Other songs, such as Psalms 40:2 and Deuteronomy 2:10, appear for the first time in the archive during this show [2]. The band provided spoken introductions for multiple songs, including Cotton, Enoch 18:14, and the band's entrance [1]. This recording is the only available capture of the event, taped and transferred by Thomas J Hartnett [1]. It is the 146th show in the archive's collection for the performer, following a previous session at The Current [2].",
